Create billing services for ISAFlow Admin Platform Phase 2. These services manage plans, subscriptions, and invoices.

## Existing Patterns

Read existing services at `src/modules/admin/services/` to match the exact pattern:
- `import { sql } from '@/lib/neon';`
- `import { log } from '@/lib/logger';`
- Types from `@/modules/admin/types/admin.types.ts`
- `type Row = any` with eslint disable
- Tagged template literals for all SQL
- Whitelist-based `sql.unsafe()` for sort columns only

## Existing Database Tables (already migrated)

**plans** — id, code, name, description, monthly_price_cents, annual_price_cents, currency, features (JSONB), limits (JSONB), is_active, display_order, created_at, updated_at

**subscriptions** — id, company_id, plan_id, status (trial/active/past_due/cancelled/paused), billing_cycle (monthly/annual), current_period_start, current_period_end, cancel_at_period_end, cancelled_at, stripe_subscription_id, discount_percent, notes, created_at, updated_at

**admin_invoices** — id, company_id, subscription_id, invoice_number (unique), status (draft/sent/paid/overdue/cancelled/credited), subtotal_cents, tax_cents, total_cents, currency, due_date, paid_at, payment_method, stripe_invoice_id, line_items (JSONB), notes, created_at

## Types to Add

Add these types to `src/modules/admin/types/admin.types.ts`:

```typescript
export interface Plan {
  id: string;
  code: string;
  name: string;
  description: string | null;
  monthly_price_cents: number;
  annual_price_cents: number;
  currency: string;
  features: Record<string, unknown>;
  limits: Record<string, unknown>;
  is_active: boolean;
  display_order: number;
  created_at: string;
  updated_at: string;
}

export interface SubscriptionListItem {
  id: string;
  company_id: string;
  company_name: string;
  plan_id: string;
  plan_name: string;
  plan_code: string;
  status: string;
  billing_cycle: string;
  current_period_start: string | null;
  current_period_end: string | null;
  cancel_at_period_end: boolean;
  discount_percent: number;
  monthly_amount_cents: number;
  created_at: string;
}

export interface InvoiceListItem {
  id: string;
  company_id: string;
  company_name: string;
  invoice_number: string;
  status: string;
  subtotal_cents: number;
  tax_cents: number;
  total_cents: number;
  currency: string;
  due_date: string | null;
  paid_at: string | null;
  payment_method: string | null;
  created_at: string;
}

export interface BillingOverview {
  mrr_cents: number;
  arr_cents: number;
  total_subscriptions: number;
  active_subscriptions: number;
  past_due_count: number;
  trial_count: number;
  churn_rate_percent: number;
  arpu_cents: number;
  total_revenue_cents: number;
  outstanding_cents: number;
}
```

## Files to Create

### 1. `src/modules/admin/services/planService.ts`

Functions:
- `listPlans(includeArchived?: boolean): Promise<Plan[]>` — list all plans, optionally include archived (is_active=false), ORDER BY display_order
- `getPlan(planId: string): Promise<Plan | null>` — get single plan by ID
- `createPlan(data: { code: string; name: string; description?: string; monthly_price_cents: number; annual_price_cents: number; currency?: string; features?: Record<string,unknown>; limits?: Record<string,unknown>; display_order?: number }): Promise<Plan>` — insert and return
- `updatePlan(planId: string, data: Partial<Plan>): Promise<void>` — update fields dynamically. Build SET clause from provided fields. Only allow updating: name, description, monthly_price_cents, annual_price_cents, currency, features, limits, is_active, display_order
- `archivePlan(planId: string): Promise<void>` — set is_active = false

### 2. `src/modules/admin/services/billingService.ts`

Functions:
- `getBillingOverview(): Promise<BillingOverview>` — aggregate metrics:
  - MRR: SUM of monthly amounts for active subscriptions (if annual, divide by 12)
  - ARR: MRR * 12
  - Count active, past_due, trial subscriptions
  - Churn rate: cancelled in last 30 days / total active at start of period * 100
  - ARPU: MRR / active subscriptions
  - Total revenue: SUM of paid invoices
  - Outstanding: SUM of sent+overdue invoices

- `listSubscriptions(filters: { status?: string; plan_id?: string; search?: string; page?: number; limit?: number }): Promise<PaginatedResult<SubscriptionListItem>>` — JOIN companies and plans, support filters and pagination

- `getSubscription(subscriptionId: string): Promise<SubscriptionListItem | null>`

- `createSubscription(data: { company_id: string; plan_id: string; billing_cycle: string; discount_percent?: number; notes?: string }): Promise<string>` — insert, set current_period_start=NOW(), calculate current_period_end (30 days for monthly, 365 for annual), return id

- `updateSubscription(subscriptionId: string, data: { plan_id?: string; billing_cycle?: string; discount_percent?: number; status?: string; notes?: string }): Promise<void>`

- `cancelSubscription(subscriptionId: string, atPeriodEnd: boolean): Promise<void>` — if atPeriodEnd, set cancel_at_period_end=true; else set status='cancelled', cancelled_at=NOW()

- `listInvoices(filters: { company_id?: string; status?: string; from_date?: string; to_date?: string; search?: string; page?: number; limit?: number }): Promise<PaginatedResult<InvoiceListItem>>` — JOIN companies, support filters

- `createInvoice(data: { company_id: string; subscription_id?: string; subtotal_cents: number; tax_cents: number; total_cents: number; due_date?: string; line_items?: unknown[]; notes?: string }): Promise<string>` — auto-generate invoice_number as 'INV-YYYYMM-XXXX' (sequential), return id

- `markInvoicePaid(invoiceId: string, paymentMethod: string): Promise<void>` — set status='paid', paid_at=NOW(), payment_method

- `sendInvoice(invoiceId: string): Promise<void>` — set status='sent' (actual email sending is a future concern)

Keep files under 300 lines each. Use the exact same code style as the existing admin services.

