Implement the Command Palette and Global Search for ISAFlow (WS-3.1 from PRD).

Read the PRD at /home/hein/Workspace/IsaFlow/PRD-MARNEWECK-ROADMAP.md for full specs.

## 1. Service — `src/modules/accounting/services/globalSearchService.ts`

Read existing service patterns from `src/modules/accounting/services/chartOfAccountsService.ts`.

```typescript
import { sql } from '@/lib/neon';
import { log } from '@/lib/logger';

interface SearchResult {
  type: string;        // 'customer', 'supplier', 'gl_account', 'invoice', 'journal_entry', 'bank_transaction', 'item'
  id: string;
  title: string;       // Primary display text
  subtitle: string;    // Secondary info
  url: string;         // Navigation URL
  icon: string;        // Lucide icon name
}

export async function globalSearch(companyId: string, query: string, limit: number = 8): Promise<SearchResult[]>
```

Implementation:
- Run parallel queries across 7 entity tables using Promise.all()
- Each query uses ILIKE for fuzzy matching on key fields
- Limit results per entity type to prevent one type dominating
- Company-scoped (all queries filter by company_id)

Search sources:
1. **GL Accounts**: `SELECT id, account_code, account_name, account_type FROM gl_accounts WHERE company_id = $1 AND (account_code ILIKE $2 OR account_name ILIKE $2) AND is_active = true LIMIT 3`
   - title: "{code} — {name}", subtitle: "{type}", url: "/accounting?tab=accounts", icon: "book-open"

2. **Customers**: `SELECT id, name, account_number FROM customers WHERE company_id = $1 AND (name ILIKE $2 OR account_number ILIKE $2) LIMIT 3`
   - Check if deleted_at column exists, if so add `AND deleted_at IS NULL`
   - title: "{name}", subtitle: "{account_number}", url: "/accounting/customers?id={id}", icon: "users"

3. **Suppliers**: Same pattern as customers
   - url: "/accounting/suppliers?id={id}", icon: "truck"

4. **Customer Invoices**: `SELECT id, invoice_number, customer_name, total FROM customer_invoices WHERE company_id = $1 AND (invoice_number ILIKE $2 OR customer_name ILIKE $2) LIMIT 3`
   - title: "{invoice_number}", subtitle: "{customer_name} | R {total}", url: "/accounting/customer-invoices?id={id}", icon: "file-text"

5. **Journal Entries**: `SELECT id, entry_number, description FROM gl_journal_entries WHERE company_id = $1 AND (entry_number ILIKE $2 OR description ILIKE $2) LIMIT 3`
   - title: "{entry_number}", subtitle: "{description}", url: "/accounting/journal-entries?id={id}", icon: "scroll"

6. **Bank Transactions**: `SELECT id, description, reference, amount FROM bank_transactions WHERE company_id = $1 AND (description ILIKE $2 OR reference ILIKE $2) LIMIT 3`
   - title: "{description}", subtitle: "R {amount} | {reference}", url: "/accounting/bank-transactions", icon: "landmark"

7. **Items**: `SELECT id, item_code, item_name FROM items WHERE company_id = $1 AND (item_code ILIKE $2 OR item_name ILIKE $2) LIMIT 3`
   - title: "{item_code} — {item_name}", url: "/accounting/items?id={id}", icon: "package"

Wrap the search term with `%` for ILIKE: `%${query}%`

Also export a function for quick actions:
```typescript
export function getQuickActions(): Array<{ label: string; url: string; shortcut?: string; icon: string }> {
  return [
    { label: 'New Customer Invoice', url: '/accounting/customer-invoices/new', shortcut: 'Ctrl+Shift+I', icon: 'file-plus' },
    { label: 'New Journal Entry', url: '/accounting/journal-entries/new', shortcut: 'Ctrl+Shift+J', icon: 'plus-circle' },
    { label: 'New Customer', url: '/accounting/customers/new', icon: 'user-plus' },
    { label: 'New Supplier', url: '/accounting/suppliers/new', icon: 'truck' },
    { label: 'Bank Reconciliation', url: '/accounting/bank-reconciliation', icon: 'check-square' },
    { label: 'Reports', url: '/accounting/reports', icon: 'bar-chart-2' },
  ];
}
```

## 2. API Endpoint — `pages/api/accounting/global-search.ts`

Read existing API pattern from `pages/api/accounting/journal-entries.ts`.

- GET: `?q=searchterm&limit=8`
- Uses withCompany + withErrorHandler
- Returns: `{ success: true, data: { results: SearchResult[], actions: QuickAction[] } }`
- If q is empty or too short (<2 chars), return only actions (no search)

## 3. UI Component — `src/components/layout/CommandPalette.tsx`

This is a modal overlay component. Read `src/components/layout/AppLayout.tsx` to understand how to integrate.

```tsx
// Structure:
// - Dark backdrop overlay (onClick closes)
// - Centered dialog (max-w-xl, rounded, shadow)
// - Search input at top (auto-focused on open)
// - Results list below (scrollable, max-h-96)
// - Keyboard navigation: ArrowUp/Down, Enter, Esc

import { useState, useEffect, useRef, useCallback } from 'react';
import { useRouter } from 'next/router';
import { useCompany } from '@/contexts/CompanyContext';
import { apiFetch } from '@/lib/apiFetch';
import { Search, X, ArrowRight, ... } from 'lucide-react'; // use appropriate icons

interface CommandPaletteProps {
  isOpen: boolean;
  onClose: () => void;
}
```

Features:
- Search input with debounce (300ms)
- When empty: show "Quick Actions" section and "Recent Items" (from localStorage key `isaflow_recent_items`)
- When typing: show search results grouped by entity type
- Each result shows icon, title, subtitle, type badge
- Arrow keys navigate, Enter opens selected, Esc closes
- Clicking a result navigates and closes
- Save visited items to localStorage recent items (max 10)

Styling: Use Tailwind classes with CSS vars for dark/light mode support:
- Backdrop: `fixed inset-0 bg-black/50 z-50`
- Dialog: `bg-[var(--ff-bg-primary)] border border-[var(--ff-border-light)] rounded-xl shadow-2xl`
- Input: `w-full px-4 py-3 text-lg bg-transparent border-b border-[var(--ff-border-light)]`
- Results: scrollable list with hover highlight

## 4. Integration in AppLayout

Read `src/components/layout/AppLayout.tsx` and add:
1. State: `const [commandPaletteOpen, setCommandPaletteOpen] = useState(false);`
2. Global keydown listener for Ctrl+K (or Cmd+K on Mac):
```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  const handler = (e: KeyboardEvent) => {
    if ((e.ctrlKey || e.metaKey) && e.key === 'k') {
      e.preventDefault();
      setCommandPaletteOpen(prev => !prev);
    }
  };
  window.addEventListener('keydown', handler);
  return () => window.removeEventListener('keydown', handler);
}, []);
```
3. Render `<CommandPalette isOpen={commandPaletteOpen} onClose={() => setCommandPaletteOpen(false)} />` at the end of AppLayout

IMPORTANT: Follow all ISAFlow patterns. Tailwind + CSS vars for styling. apiFetch for API calls. useCompany for company context.

